      "code": "ai1_offset_y[1] = ps_sao->b4_y_offset_1;\nai1_offset_y[2] = ps_sao->b4_y_offset_2;\nai1_offset_y[3] = ps_sao->b4_y_offset_3;\nai1_offset_y[4] = ps_sao->b4_y_offset_4;",
      "note": "First proved current-CTB materialization of input-derived luma SAO offsets into the vulnerable local table.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "decoder/ihevcd_sao.c",
      "function": "ihevcd_sao_shift_ctb",
      "line": null,
      "code": "WORD8 ai1_offset_y[8];",
      "note": "The staged vulnerable source declares `WORD8 ai1_offset_y[8];`, later sets only `ai1_offset_y[0]` and `ai1_offset_y[1..4]`, and never writes entries 5..7 before `_mm_loadl_epi64` reads the whole table. The patch changes this to `WORD8 ai1_offset_y[8] = {0};` and applies the same fix to the chroma tables.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "decoder/ihevcd_sao.c",
      "function": "ihevcd_sao_shift_ctb",
      "line": 573,
